// Attempt v16 generic renderer (see generic_renderer.h). DIAGNOSTIC ONLY.
// v24 (inefficiency audit, local-analysis/inefficiency-audit/report.md): same draws and state
// mapping as v23, less CPU per draw and per frame:
//  - shader pack keys and vertex-fetch decodes come from an exact-match cache of the microcode
//    bytes (generic_renderer_cpu.h) instead of being recomputed for every draw;
//  - a texture binding (fetch words -> image, sampler) is verified against guest memory once per
//    frame instead of once per draw (32 guest reads each); assumption: a texture's bytes do not
//    change between two draws of one frame (v23 would re-upload such a texture mid-frame);
//  - vertex bytes are swapped straight into the upload ring (one vectorized pass), indices are
//    clamped and bounded in one pass;
//  - two frame slots: present() submits frame N and returns frame N-1's image (one frame of
//    latency; the GPU runs frame N while the CPU records N+1); readback from host-cached memory.
// Runtime switches (checked every 30 presents): files/private-trace/diag-generic-sync restores the
// v23 synchronous present, files/private-trace/diag-generic-nocache the v23 per-draw hashing and
// texture verification. RENDER_GENERIC_TIMING (every 60 presents) reports where the time went.
// v40 (rendering audit; local-analysis/rendering-audit/v40-against-v35.diff):
//  - resolves follow 823C2738's flags: 0x200 clears depth/stencil (f1, stack word 92), clears cover
//    the 8-aligned resolve rectangle only (Xenia GetResolveInfo), 0x2000 (copy command null) and
//    mip/slice destinations do not overwrite the base image, and a resolved view compensates the
//    red/blue swap 823C2970..823C2AB8 applies when the destination's red selector is not X;
//  - EDRAM targets are keyed by storage format (Xenia GetStorageColorFormat: 10 = 2, 12 = 3; 1
//    stores 0's bytes) and a resolve reads the most recently written target at its base;
//  - rasterizer state: PA_SU_VTX_CNTL half-pixel offset, PA_SU_SC_MODE_CNTL cull/face and
//    polygon offset; Clear intersects the D3D scissor (823D89A8);
//  - (texture sampling) an undecodable 2D fetch samples its swizzle's constant selectors;
//  - files/private-trace/diag-frame-census: a one-frame census (see generic_renderer.h), and the
//    A/B switches diag-generic-legacy-raster / diag-generic-legacy-resolve (v35 behaviour).
// v73 (flicker/artifact audit): the tile-row bands in the upper screen (v70-play-1.png) are the ambient light grid
// (DrawVertices rect lists, VS 93adf129/c145e5ab) reading TEXCOORD0 by vertex index from guest memory that no resolve
// writes, instead of the resolved 80x45 tile classification at the index POSITION.w * 64 + POSITION.z
// (resolved_vertex_fetch.h). The attribute is now gathered on the GPU from the resolved image (recordGather,
// generic_vertex_gather.hlsl); files/private-trace/diag-generic-no-resolved-vertex-fetch restores v72. Diagnostics:
// files/private-trace/diag-census-points (census probe points), diag-generic-frame-stats (16 presents of
// per-tile-row block means), notes vertex-stream-from-resolve / vertex-gather-refused, census VG lines.
// v85 (transparency and blending audit against the v67 census; local-analysis/attempts/v85):
//  - late depth/stencil tests for draws whose pixel shader can discard while they write depth or stencil:
//    every pack pixel shader declares EarlyFragmentTests (XenosRecomp's [earlydepthstencil]), under which
//    Vulkan writes depth/stencil before the shader's kill (cutout hair/decals, fences, shadow cutouts,
//    im.fxc #73's stencil mask); such a draw gets the module without that mode (spirv_alpha_test.h);
//  - all eight RB_COLORCONTROL alpha functions (the pack's test is GEQUAL only; GTA V also uses GREATER,
//    NOTEQUAL and LEQUAL) and alpha to mask with one sample (xenos_alpha_state.h);
//  - blending is not enabled on a 32-bit float target the device cannot blend (xenos_blend_state.h).
//  Switches (every 30 presents): diag-generic-early-tests (v71: EarlyFragmentTests kept), diag-generic-
//  legacy-alpha (v71 alpha test, alpha to mask ignored), diag-generic-no-a2c, diag-generic-legacy-blend.
// v86 (HUD/UI, ui_texture_tracking.h): textures the CPU rewrites in place (the Scaleform glyph cache) are
// re-read after their unlock (invalidateMemory, diag-ui-no-unlock-invalidate restores v71) and textures a
// Scaleform pixel shader samples are verified by a hash of every byte once per frame instead of the
// 32-word sample (diag-ui-sampled-fingerprint restores v71). RENDER_GENERIC_UI reports both.
// v100 integration of v75 (desk noise/exposure) and v79 (post-processing), which both wrote small resolves back to
// guest memory and both made the 7e3 resolve continuous:
//  - resolve writeback: v75's (generic_resolve_writeback.h): queued per slot, taken out after the fence, published in
//    present() inside the present hook's executor gate through the registry's validated publication at the
//    destination owner's own mapping (the path the native renderer's RENDER_API_LIVE_RESOLVE publication uses),
//    <= 4096 texels, level 0 / layer 0; files/private-trace/diag-generic-no-resolve-writeback restores v71,
//    diag-generic-writeback-1x1-only (v79's switch) limits it to 1x1 destinations. v79's direct stores into the
//    0xA0000000 view (no owner check, from waitSlot while guest threads run) are not used.
//  - continuous 7e3: v75's encode7e3Continuous (mode 3, generic_hdr7e3.hlsli): /1023 like mode 1, so it equals
//    mode 1 at every exact 7e3 value; NaN and negatives give 0. diag-generic-hdr-quantized (v75) and
//    diag-generic-hardware-7e3 (v79's name) both restore v71's mode 1. v79's precise7e3 (/1024) is not used.
//  - v79 kept: the display gamma ramp D3DDevice_SetGammaRamp keeps (setGammaRamp, hook 836AFAF8) maps the presented
//    RGB like the 360 scan-out LUT (diag-generic-no-gamma-ramp restores v71); RENDER_POSTFX lines (a listed postfx
//    shader's first draw, then at most once per 300 frames) and a census line per draw with c18 = globalScalars3 and
//    the listed postfx shaders' registers, tagged "PF" here (v79 called it PC; v76's shadow-draw PC lines keep PC).
//  - v75 kept: RENDER_GENERIC_EXPOSURE_STATE (renderer_boundary_trace.cpp), census gs3= on D lines, probes p8-p11.
// v96 (long-session stability, on v99 = v71 + v74 + v72 + v76 + v80): v71 kept every texture (keyed by fetch words, so
// every streamed address stays), target, resolve destination, spare, framebuffer and pipeline for the whole
// session; a target resize dropped every framebuffer handle without destroying it; pending EDRAM alias clears
// of a target that is never bound again appended rectangles every frame. v74 added texture eviction above
// 1.5 GB (the v74 device run: 606 textures = 142 MB decoded, so it never ran). v96 (maintain(), at presents):
//  - textures unused for textureMaxAge frames are destroyed, and the least recently used (unused for at
//    least textureMinAge frames) whenever the count (2048), bytes (512 MB) or, with VK_EXT_memory_budget,
//    90% of the heap budget is exceeded; targets, resolve destinations and pipelines likewise but only above
//    their soft limits (which the observed scenes stay below); resolve destinations with a v74 shape (cube,
//    layers, mips) that nothing wrote or sampled for shapedMaxAge frames are freed; retired resolve spares
//    age out; framebuffers are destroyed with their attachments and after framebufferMaxAge unused frames;
//  - pending alias clears of one value merge without duplicate rectangles (and flush past 512);
//  - descriptor pools flush the frame before they run out; failed allocations clean up after themselves;
//  - the display gone (30 failed displays in a row: displayResult) stops the per-frame blit and CPU readback
//    until a probing present every 30 displays again; the present images are freed meanwhile;
//  - RENDER_GENERIC_RESOURCES (every 150 presents): object counts, bytes per category, allocations,
//    evictions, heap budget/usage and the process RSS.
// files/private-trace/diag-generic-v99-resources restores v99 for all of it (v74's 1.5 GB texture policy;
// the log line stays), and diag-generic-no-{texture,target,resolved,pipeline}-evict / -no-framebuffer-trim /
// -no-clear-dedup / -no-pool-guard / -no-display-lost each one part; RENDER_GENERIC_V96_MODE reports the state.
