    // ---- lane fsr-stage-b (present_source.h): render-resolution stage B. With a scale applied, a frame that goes to the
    // presenter on the GPU is handed over at its render size (rsbW x rsbH) instead of through stage A's 1280x720 present
    // image; the presenter scales that to the window in one step. files/private-trace/diag-rs-stage-a (read once, here, and
    // only when a scale is applied) keeps stage A's path for an A/B. rsbW = 0: stage A / no scale; present() then computes
    // v463's sizes. Out of line and noexcept: present() keeps its control flow (and its profile record). The two values are
    // static (one renderer per process, as the presenter): a member here would move every later member of Renderer and so
    // change the encoding of the hot functions that address them (draw() came out 520 bytes larger with members).
